<section id="faq" class="px-4 py-16 bg-background-black md:px-8">
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center content-container">
    <div class="mb-16 pill">
      <p class="">Common questions</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mb-12 max-w-2xl text-2xl font-bold text-center text-white sm:text-3xl">Founder FAQ</h2>

    <div class="space-y-4 w-full max-w-3xl">
      <details class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 group">
        <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-semibold list-none text-white cursor-pointer">
          How long does MVP development take?
          <span class="ml-4 transition-transform text-secondary group-open:rotate-180">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/70">Most MVPs take 8–16 weeks depending on scope and complexity. We start with a scoping call to understand your goals, then provide a realistic timeline before we write a single line of code. We scope to what validates your idea, not what looks impressive in a deck.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 group">
        <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-semibold list-none text-white cursor-pointer">
          How much does MVP development cost?
          <span class="ml-4 transition-transform text-secondary group-open:rotate-180">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/70">MVP projects typically range from $15K–$60K+ depending on the product. We price based on scope, not hours, so you get a fixed deliverable with no surprise invoices. We'll give you a clear estimate after our discovery call.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 group">
        <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-semibold list-none text-white cursor-pointer">
          Do you work with early-stage startups?
          <span class="ml-4 transition-transform text-secondary group-open:rotate-180">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/70">Yes. Early-stage startups are our primary focus. We work with pre-seed through Series A founders, typically 1–10 person teams who need a technical partner rather than a traditional agency. We're built for founder speed.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 group">
        <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-semibold list-none text-white cursor-pointer">
          Can you help us refactor an existing prototype?
          <span class="ml-4 transition-transform text-secondary group-open:rotate-180">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/70">Absolutely. Prototype-to-production refactoring is one of our most common engagements. We audit your existing codebase, identify the highest-risk areas, and refactor in a way that keeps your product live while building a foundation you can scale on.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 group">
        <summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-semibold list-none text-white cursor-pointer">
          Do you work with Canadian startups outside Toronto?
          <span class="ml-4 transition-transform text-secondary group-open:rotate-180">▼</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/70">Yes. We work with Canadian startups coast to coast: Vancouver, Calgary, Montreal, Ottawa, and beyond. We're fully remote-first and designed to work with distributed founding teams wherever they are.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="book-a-call" class="px-4 py-16 bg-background-navy md:px-8">
